# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Muyu Lu et al. (2026). OMC-bench and AtomBit-OMC: task-aligned benchmarks and robust, interpretable machine-learned interatomic potentials for organic molecular crystals.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-026-02315-3
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 28a4fb5b45440677...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 556 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lu2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the OMC training dataset (PBE-D3(BJ), CSD-derived
# organic molecular crystals: optimization trajectories, AIMD and fixed
# displacements), 14 off-the-shelf foundation MLIPs as distributed and
# five OMC-specialized models trained from scratch (NEMP-OMC, MACE-OMC,
# MatRIS-OMC, AtomBit-OMC-s, AtomBit-OMC-l); Task 1 force and stress
# MAEs of Table 1. Phonon, thermodynamic, cocrystal-recovery and
# polymorph-ranking metrics (Tasks 2-4) are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-lu2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Lu et al. (2026): OMC-bench task-aligned benchmarks for organic molecular crystals and the AtomBit-OMC Cartesian-tensor MLIP" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-lu2026 .

