###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Data generation consumed about 1.3e7 CPU core-hours and 2.0e5 GPU-hours (Methods). AtomBit models were trained in FP32 on 8 GPUs for 15 epochs.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Off-the-shelf checkpoints are paper-local runs (names as printed; none matches a registry model version). Their pretraining data may overlap OMC-bench (documented for UMA-md). Tasks 2-4 metrics are not energy/force/stress errors and are not encoded. The OMC dataset size is printed as 2.07 M; no n.
# - AtomBit is a new registry method (origin lu2026); Eqnorm is a new registry method without origin (its paper is not in the corpus).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lu2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

